// moveData.js — Mochiichao arena move data, REAL move names + mechanics
// (CORRECTION BATCH, 2026-10-25; corrects PR #35's genericized move
// vocabulary — see REPLACEMENTS.md, Correction section).
//
// WHAT IS VERBATIM (from decomp extraction already on main):
//   name, type, category, power, accuracy, pp, priority, effect —
//   copied field-for-field from src/lib/generated/decomp_black2_moves.json
//   (560 moves, Black 2 decomp extraction; that file's own source note
//   names its decomp origin). No value in those fields was re-typed,
//   re-balanced, or rounded by this module. Accuracy 101 in the source
//   is the source's never-miss marker; it is kept verbatim and flagged
//   as neverMisses, not rewritten to 100. Power 1 in the source (38
//   moves) is the source's placeholder for fixed/variable damage —
//   the effect field states the real rule (level damage, 40 flat,
//   halve HP, equalise HP, random damage, Bide storage); it is NOT
//   1 point of damage, and this module does not reinterpret it.
//   Move names are move names: they are NOT creature names, and this
//   file contains zero creature names (verified: no Black 2 move name
//   equals, or contains as a whole word, any Black 2 species name —
//   0/560 exact matches, 0/560 word matches, checked against
//   decomp_black2_species.json, 650 names).
//
// WHAT COMES FROM THE FIRERED ERA (labelled, never mixed into Black 2
// values — the two generations differ, e.g. Tackle is 35 power / 95
// accuracy in FireRed vs 50 / 100 in Black 2, Protect priority 3 vs 4,
// so FireRed values NEVER overwrite Black 2 fields):
//   target, makesContact, effectChance — from
//   src/lib/generated/decomp_firered_moves.json (354 moves), joined on
//   sourceConstant for 351 of the 560 moves; the other 209 moves have
//   no FireRed row and carry null for all three fields. effectChance
//   is FireRed's secondaryEffectChance (e.g. Flamethrower 10, Toxic
//   100); Black 2 extraction carries no chance field, so no Black 2
//   chance is claimed anywhere here.
//   animScriptFirered — the per-move animation script label from
//   FireRed's data/battle_anim_scripts.s, gBattleAnims_Moves table
//   (356 entries = Move_NONE + 354 moves + Move_COUNT; table order
//   matches the FireRed moves order, verified entry-by-entry).
//   Only the table label is carried (e.g. Move_TACKLE); no script
//   body, no graphic, no sound from that file is included.
//   Bide note: FireRed flags Bide as contact AND targets USER; this
//   module lets target win (shape self) — a waiting move is not a
//   dash, whatever its contact flag says.
//
// WHAT IS ARENA DERIVATION (Mochiichao staging, NOT decomp data —
// labelled as such wherever it appears, and never presented as source
// values):
//   * shape / rangeU / motion / shapeBasis — the fanMechanics.js
//     aim-shape vocabulary (lane / wedge / zone / self / beam / dash),
//     assigned by the ordered rule recorded per move in shapeBasis
//     (status self-target -> self, field/hazard status -> zone,
//     contact + priority -> dash, switch/charge effects -> dash,
//     spread names/effects -> zone, Flamethrower + Heat Wave -> wedge,
//     Beam/Cannon/Pulse names and recharge effects -> beam, contact
//     damage -> melee, everything else damage -> lane, aimed status
//     -> lane). Shape counts: lane 325, melee 107, self 81, zone 20,
//     beam 19, dash 6, wedge 2.
//   * element — the 12 True Element map from elementImpactVfx.js
//     (LEGACY_MOVE_TYPE_TO_ELEMENT). 15 of 17 Black 2 types map;
//     ICE (20 moves) and ROCK (15 moves) have NO entry in that map,
//     so those 35 moves keep their own element name and
//     elementMappedToTrue: false, with a generic puff/none impact
//     until the True Element unification lands. Nothing was invented
//     to force them into a True Element.
//   * impact — shape + ring only, from elementImpactVfx.js's family
//     table for mapped elements (colours live in that module; the
//     game looks them up by element). No sound identifiers, no art,
//     no dialogue in this file.
//   * timing — battleTreatments.js TIMING verbatim for every move:
//     windup 250 ms, strike (impact hold) 90 ms, follow-through
//     700 ms (recoil 300 + recover 400), total 1040 ms. Priority is
//     preserved as the priority field for turn order; it does not
//     alter these presentation numbers in this module.
//   * frame data — the SAME treatments timing expressed at 60 fps in
//     industry-standard startup / active / recovery vocabulary:
//     startupFrames 15 (250 ms), activeFrames 5 (90 ms = 5.4 frames,
//     rounded to 5), recoveryFrames 42 (700 ms), totalFrames 62
//     (1040 ms = 62.4 frames, rounded to 62; 15 + 5 + 42 = 62).
//     No per-move frame table from any other game is claimed.
//   * economy — pp verbatim; arenaUses = max(5, round(pp x 1.5)) x 2
//     (fanMechanics.js maxUses); cooldownMs 8000 + energyCost 50 for
//     status moves only (fanMechanics.js FAN constants); damage moves
//     carry cooldownMs 0 / energyCost 0 because fanMechanics.js defines
//     no per-damage-move realtime cooldown or energy cost — none was
//     invented here. Turn-based use is governed by pp/arenaUses.
//   * kind — fanMechanics.js movePickScore input vocabulary: damage
//     for all damaging moves; heal for restore effects, rest for Rest,
//     buff for stat-up status, status for all other status moves.
//   * effect flags — booleans read straight off the verbatim Black 2
//     effect string, so fanMechanics.js scoring can use them without
//     re-parsing effects: recoil (10 moves), multiHit (19), highCrit
//     (18), recharge (7), chargeTurn (4). Counts are from the effect
//     strings, not from playtesting.
//
// COMPATIBILITY: each entry carries the fields fanMechanics.js
// movePickScore reads (power, shape, reachU, kind, recoil, recharge,
//   — reachU aliases rangeU on every entry (added 2026-10-25: the
//   scorer reads reachU, so a rangeU-only entry scored as reach 99);
// plus sameType left to the caller, which knows the user's elements)
// and the fields arenaCombat-style staging reads (timing + frames).
// No DOM, no game imports.
// Node-testable: node --test moveData.test.js (from a directory
// without a "type": "module" package.json in scope, as with the
// other CommonJS modules in this folder).
//
// SCOPE RULE (standing, 2026-10-25): moves and animations are NOT
// replaced. The only exclusions are creature names, sounds, art, and
// dialogue — none of which is in this file.

